    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOMMiGhs8AAAABQmgrlA",
      "title": "fix: set JSON content type on simulator RPC responses",
      "author": "hehuanlu",
      "number": 427,
      "body": "<!--\nContributions welcome! See https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/.github/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md\n-->\n\n**Description**\n\n<!--\nA clear and concise description of the features you're adding in this pull request.\n-->\n\nSet `Content-Type: application/json` on successful HTTP JSON-RPC responses from the simulator. The header is added in the HTTP handler immediately before writing the encoded JSON response, so plain-text error responses and WebSocket upgrade responses keep their own response types.\n\nSome RPC consumers, including the wagmi case reported in the issue, rely on the JSON content type when parsing a successful RPC response.\n\n\n\n**Tests**\n\n<!--\nPlease describe any tests you've added. If you've added no tests, or left important behavior untested, please explain why not.\n-->\n\n- Added an in-process RPC test that sends `eth_chainId` through the simulator's HTTP handler and checks the status, JSON body, and content type.\n- `go test ./opsimulator -count=1` passes.\n- `git diff --check` passes.\n\n**Additional context**\n\n<!--\nAdd any other context about the problem you're solving.\n-->\n\n**Metadata**\n\n<!-- \nInclude a link to any github issues that this may close in the following form:\n- Fixes #[Link to Issue]\n-->\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/supersim",
      "createdAt": "2026-11-20T06:47:41Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
